    "statement": "In NSCLC_primary_tumor, GRHL1 vs TACSTD2: rho=0.445 (p=1.57e-50, n=1017, MODERATE_pos); GRHL1 vs CLDN4: rho=0.021 (p=4.96e-01, n=1017, NOT_SIGNIFICANT). On the pre-specified mixed-NSCLC slice, GRHL1 tracks TACSTD2 (TROP2) but not CLDN4 (near-zero, not significant). The shared-target claim is only half true here. Histology split (pre-specified sensitivity, not a rescue): LUAD GRHL1\u2013TACSTD2 rho=0.397 (p=7.25e-21, n=515, MODERATE_pos); LUAD GRHL1\u2013CLDN4 rho=0.391 (p=3.18e-20, n=515, MODERATE_pos); LUSC GRHL1\u2013TACSTD2 rho=0.387 (p=2.36e-19, n=502, MODERATE_pos); LUSC GRHL1\u2013CLDN4 rho=0.245 (p=2.78e-08, n=502, WEAK_pos). Pooling LUAD+LUSC can cancel a within-LUAD GRHL1\u2013CLDN4 correlation. We still score the claim on mixed NSCLC because that was the primary cohort."
